{"content":[{"c":["MICAH (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Ephraimite judge who had idols made and then hired a Levite to become his priest (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.17.1-18.31","r":"Judg.17.1-18.31","rawR":"Judg.17.1-18.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.17.1-18.31","value":"Judg.17.1-18.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 17–18"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Shimei’s descendant from Reuben’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.5","r":"1Chr.5.5","rawR":"1Chr.5.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.5","value":"1Chr.5.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Alternate spelling of Mica, Mephibosheth’s son and the great-grandson of King Saul, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.34-35","r":"1Chr.8.34-35","rawR":"1Chr.8.34-35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.34-35","value":"1Chr.8.34-35"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 8:34-35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.40-41","r":"1Chr.9.40-41","rawR":"1Chr.9.40-41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.40-41","value":"1Chr.9.40-41"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:40-41"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Mica_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Mica_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Mica_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Mica #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. KJV spelling of Mica, Zicri’s son, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.15","r":"1Chr.9.15","rawR":"1Chr.9.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.15","value":"1Chr.9.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 9:15"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Mica_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Mica_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Mica_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Mica #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Levite and Uzziel’s son from Kohath’s clan, whose temple responsibilities included care of the furniture and equipment (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.23.20","r":"1Chr.23.20","rawR":"1Chr.23.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.23.20","value":"1Chr.23.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 23:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.24-25","r":"1Chr.24.24-25","rawR":"1Chr.24.24-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.24-25","value":"1Chr.24.24-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"24:24-25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Alternate spelling of Micaiah, Acbor’s father, in ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.34.20","r":"2Chr.34.20","rawR":"2Chr.34.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.34.20","value":"2Chr.34.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chronicles 34:20"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Micaiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Micaiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Micaiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Micaiah #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. Prophet and author of the OT book that bears his name (",{"href":"?bref=Mic.1.1","r":"Mic.1.1","rawR":"Mic.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.1.1","value":"Mic.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mi 1:1"},"). A native of Moresheth, a town about 21 miles (33.8 kilometers) southwest of Jerusalem, Micah prophesied to both northern and southern kingdoms during the reigns of Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah (750–686 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). According to ",{"href":"?bref=Mic.1.9","r":"Mic.1.9","rawR":"Mic.1.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.1.9","value":"Mic.1.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Micah 1:9"},", he was still prophesying in 701 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," when the Assyrian armies under Sennacherib (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.36.1-37.38","r":"Isa.36.1-37.38","rawR":"Isa.36.1-37.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.36.1-37.38","value":"Isa.36.1-37.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 36–37"},") besieged Jerusalem. About 100 years later, Micah is used as an example of an early prophet who predicted the destruction of Jerusalem (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.26.16-19","r":"Jer.26.16-19","rawR":"Jer.26.16-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.26.16-19","value":"Jer.26.16-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 26:16-19"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MicahBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MicahBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MicahBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Micah, Book of"},"; ",{"href":"?item=ProphetProphetess_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"ProphetProphetess_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"ProphetProphetess_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Prophet, Prophetess"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"MicahPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 17–18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.17.1-18.31","rawQueryValue":"Judg.17.1-18.31","sourceRefExact":"Judg.17.1-18.31"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 5:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.5.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.5.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.5.5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 8:34-35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.8.34-35","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.8.34-35","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.8.34-35"},{"anchorText":"9:40-41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.40-41","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.40-41","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.40-41"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 9:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.15"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 23:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.23.20","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.23.20","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.23.20"},{"anchorText":"24:24-25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2